.TH SWISST 1 "September 2026" "swisst 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swisst \- provider, model and harness sync CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swisst
.RI [ provider add | provider list | provider remove ]
.br
.B swisst
.RI [ models NAME [--pick] [--json] ]
.br
.B swisst
.RI [ model add | model remove ]
.br
.B swisst
.RI [ sync [--harness ID] [--dry-run] ]
.br
.B swisst
.RI [ harness list ]
.br
.B swisst
.RI [ secret VAR ]
.br
.B swisst
.RI [ config-path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Swisst keeps one provider store
.RI ( ~/.config/swisst/swisst.json )
and renders it into every harness config (opencode, claude, codex,
gemini). API keys are kept by reference: the store holds only the
secret name, values resolve at query/sync time through the configured
secret backend.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B provider add --name NAME --base-url URL [--api openai-compatible|anthropic] [--key-env VAR] [--env-prefix PREFIX]
Register or update a provider. Key default: \fB<NAME>_API_KEY\fR.
PREFIX enables \fBPREFIX_BASE_URL\fR / \fBPREFIX_API_KEY\fR exports
for env-style harnesses.
.TP
.B provider list
Show providers with API kind, URL, key ref and pinned-model count.
.TP
.B provider remove NAME
Drop a provider from the store.
.TP
.B models NAME [--pick] [--json]
Live-enumerate \fB/v1/models\fR on an OpenAI-compatible provider.
\fB*\fR marks pinned models. \fB--pick\fR opens the ratatui
multi-select (space toggles, enter saves, q cancels) and writes the
selection to the store. \fB--json\fR prints raw JSON.
.TP
.B model add PROVIDER MODEL_ID
Pin one model id for sync.
.TP
.B model remove PROVIDER MODEL_ID
Unpin one model id.
.TP
.B sync [--harness ID] [--dry-run]
Render the store into harness configs. \fB--dry-run\fR prints actions
without writing.
.TP
.B harness list
Show harness ids, target paths and present/missing status.
.TP
.B secret VAR
Resolve one secret through the backend (length only, never prints it).
.TP
.B config-path
Print the store file path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swisst/swisst.json
Provider store (respects \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.config/swisst/harnesses/
File-backed harness templates (see harness-template-spec.md).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Config root override.
.TP
.B SWISST_HARNESS_DIR
Extra template search dirs (path-separated, earliest wins).
.TP
.B INFISICAL_PROJECT, INFISICAL_ENV
Infisical scoping fallback when the store sets no project/env.
.TP
.B <KEY_ENV> vars
Plain-env secret values; override the manager backend.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
swisst provider add --name mtplx --base-url http://192.168.1.200:8066
swisst models mtplx --pick
swisst sync --dry-run && swisst sync
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
harness-template-spec.md, README.md, docs/zoid-shell.md
